Hello Mr. Bratberg! Here is a simple guide to the current game:
On the title screen, the only button that is unimplemented as of right now is the Towers menu button. Everything else has content you can look at.
In the next screen, there is a LOT going on. You can choose to either load a game, or create a new one.
I have already created some saved games from before, and they can be found inside of the game_saves folder within the project.
To load a game, simply choose one of the codes from that folder and type it in correctly, or create your own game, look for the new code in the folder, then load it up later! I still need to add a feature that allows the user to actually see their code while playing, so that they can save it for later.
You've played the game already, most of the mechanics are the same. Difficulties affect number of lives/cash.
For your testing purposes, I would highly recommend choosing my newly added "sandbox" mode. It gives you infinite cash and lives, as well as the ability to try any tower with any upgrade, spawn any singular balloon, or play any of the current waves. Basically, it should hold all of the current game features as of right now.
Of course, the game isn't perfect, and you will probably run into a few problems here or there. The "Half Bumps" map is really laggy for some reason, as an example.
Thanks!
